1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,394
Hello everyone

2
00:00:06,394 --> 00:00:12,789
I am Prince Pundir, and welcome to the presentation of SafeWalk RaahSaathi, an autonomous, AI-grounded women's safety navigation platform

3
00:00:12,789 --> 00:00:19,183
Every evening, millions of women commute home from universities, corporate offices, and transit hubs

4
00:00:19,183 --> 00:00:25,577
When they open standard navigation apps, every major service optimizes for one single dimension: speed

5
00:00:25,577 --> 00:00:31,971
Distance divided by time

6
00:00:31,971 --> 00:00:38,366
They will gladly route a woman walking alone late at night through an unlit underpass or an isolated alley just to save ninety seconds

7
00:00:38,366 --> 00:00:44,760
SafeWalk redefines navigation by prioritizing human safety, combining verified road geometry, assistance havens, and explainable spatial intelligence

8
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:52,172
Before seeing the live app, look under the hood

9
00:00:52,172 --> 00:00:59,584
Conventional safety apps rely on subjective user ratings

10
00:00:59,584 --> 00:01:06,996
SafeWalk introduces a deterministic four-pillar route scoring engine

11
00:01:06,996 --> 00:01:14,408
We compute verified streetlight illumination from OpenStreetMap surveys, natural commercial footfall from active late-night storefronts and chemists, a continuous diurnal temporal penalty for night journeys, and community-verified incident reports

12
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:21,820
Furthermore, our spatial segmenter slices walking routes into 100 to 200 meter atomic sections, providing full audit transparency rather than a single black-box score

13
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:28,152
Here is SafeWalk in action

14
00:01:28,152 --> 00:01:34,483
When planning a walk in Dehradun at 10 PM, our dual-route engine renders two paths: the coral dashed line is the shortest path, but it traverses dangerous low-lit stretches

15
00:01:34,483 --> 00:01:40,815
The emerald line is our Safest Route

16
00:01:40,815 --> 00:01:47,147
Notice the Segment-Level Deep Dive card: each segment explains its score in plain language, such as eight commercial storefronts offsetting missing streetlights

17
00:01:47,147 --> 00:01:53,478
Most importantly, we strictly separate safety score from data confidence

18
00:01:53,478 --> 00:01:59,810
A road with zero reports is never falsely labeled safe: it is marked as low confidence until verified

19
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:06,582
What happens if a woman feels uncomfortable, followed, or in distress during her commute

20
00:02:06,582 --> 00:02:13,353
She does not have time to browse web directories

21
00:02:13,353 --> 00:02:20,125
She opens SafeStops

22
00:02:20,125 --> 00:02:26,897
SafeStops indexes vetted assistance havens: 24/7 police stations, campus security desks, emergency trauma centers, and verified pharmacies

23
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:33,668
We enforce strict data provenance: public datasets are marked Public Facility, while university security booths are labeled Partner-Verified

24
00:02:33,668 --> 00:02:40,440
With one single tap on Navigate to Nearest Help Point, SafeWalk calculates the safest walking path directly to the closest safe haven with instant phone links

25
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:47,736
For lone journeys, users activate Live Journey Guardian

26
00:02:47,736 --> 00:02:55,032
Designed with privacy by default, the user gives explicit consent and chooses her check-in interval, for example every five minutes with a two-minute grace period

27
00:02:55,032 --> 00:03:02,328
SafeWalk issues a high-entropy 32-byte cryptographic sharing token, storing hashes using SHA-256 and never exposing database IDs

28
00:03:02,328 --> 00:03:09,624
Periodic prompts confirm user safety

29
00:03:09,624 --> 00:03:16,920
If a check-in is missed, our server triggers simulated alerts with GPS coordinates to trusted contacts, who can tap I am responding to confirm help is underway

30
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:23,562
On the Live Guardian dashboard, you can see the active session in real-time

31
00:03:23,562 --> 00:03:30,205
The user sees the remaining grace period, battery-efficient tracking, and emergency panic buttons

32
00:03:30,205 --> 00:03:36,847
In our simulated contact viewer, trusted family members and campus security can monitor the journey securely without creating user accounts

33
00:03:36,847 --> 00:03:43,490
The moment an alert is acknowledged, the user interface updates with an empathetic confirmation badge

34
00:03:43,490 --> 00:03:50,834
Filling out forms in the dark is frustrating and slow

35
00:03:50,834 --> 00:03:58,178
SafeWalk supports Multilingual AI Voice Reporting

36
00:03:58,178 --> 00:04:05,522
Users speak naturally in Hindi, English, or Hinglish: for example, Bus stand ke paas light nahi jal rahi hai aur raat mein bahut andhera rehta hai

37
00:04:05,522 --> 00:04:12,866
Our NLP engine classifies the incident category, extracts a normalized draft, and requires user confirmation before saving

38
00:04:12,866 --> 00:04:20,210
Even in basement parking or low-signal zones, our PWA offline queue stores reports locally with cryptographic idempotency keys, syncing seamlessly once online

39
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:25,470
Finally, SafeWalk empowers campus administrations and municipal authorities through our Safety Intelligence Dashboard

40
00:04:25,470 --> 00:04:30,730
All statistics are computed live from active database records

41
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:35,990
Authorities can monitor infrastructure gaps like recurring streetlight outages and examine privacy-preserving 1

42
00:04:35,990 --> 00:04:41,250
1-kilometer spatial clusters without compromising individual travel histories

43
00:04:41,250 --> 00:04:46,510
SafeWalk RaahSaathi bridges the gap between raw maps and genuine peace of mind

44
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:51,770
Every woman deserves the safest journey home

45
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:57,030
Once again, I am Prince Pundir, and thank you for watching
